# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/slice_2a.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event slice_ward_lesson
# en: The First Ward
title [bb9ea0] = 第一道护界
# en: Professor Thorne holds up a hand and the lamplight bends around it into a pale shell. "A ward," he says. "{~It stops one blow.|One blow. That's all it ever stops.} Learn it properly or not at all."
text [df5c56] = 索恩教授抬起一只手，灯光绕着它弯成一层苍白的护壳。“护界，”他说，“{~它能挡一击。|一击。它永远只挡得住一击。}要么好好学，要么别学。”
# en: An office lit by one lamp, an old professor holding a pale shell of light between his palms like a soap bubble.
scene [86947c] = 一间只点着一盏灯的办公室，一位老教授在两掌之间托着一层苍白的光壳，像一个肥皂泡。
# en: Practise until it holds
opt.left.label [ca9f8f] = 练到它撑得住为止
# en: By midnight your shell holds for a full breath. Thorne says "Hm," which from him is a standing ovation.
opt.left.say.1 [1c452f] = 到午夜，你的护壳能撑满一整口气。索恩说了声“嗯”——从他嘴里出来，这相当于全场起立鼓掌。
# en: Ask about the theory first
opt.right.label [e6ac23] = 先问问原理
# en: He talks for an hour about lattices and intent. You understand perhaps a third of it. "Come back when the third is a half," he says.
opt.right.say.1 [75d35a] = 他讲了一个小时的晶格与意图。你大概听懂了三分之一。“等这三分之一变成一半再来，”他说。

@event slice_candle_flame
# en: Borrowed Fire
title [f667df] = 借来的火
# en: Lyra watches you fail to light a candle for the third time. "You're asking it," she says. "Fire doesn't want to be asked. {rel(lyra) >= 12: Here — watch my hand.|Watch, if you can keep up.}"
text [8ed13c] = 莱拉看着你第三次没能点燃蜡烛。“你在请求它，”她说，“火不喜欢被请求。{rel(lyra) >= 12: 来——看我的手。|看好了，如果你跟得上的话。}”
# en: A crimson-haired student balancing a flame on one fingertip while another student squints at a sputtering candle.
scene [7237b8] = 一个绯红头发的学生指尖托着一簇火苗，另一个学生眯眼盯着一根噼啪作响的蜡烛。
# en: Watch her hand
opt.left.label [8f7d80] = 看她的手
# en: She doesn't explain. She just does it, slowly, twice. On the third try your candle catches, and so, very briefly, does your sleeve.
opt.left.say.1 [59ceef] = 她不解释，只是慢慢地做了两遍。第三次，你的蜡烛点着了——你的袖子也短暂地着了一下。
# en: Challenge her to teach you properly
opt.right.label [02abfd] = 激她好好教你
# en: You hold your own long enough that she stops and actually explains. "Fine," she says. "You'll do."
opt.right.say.1 [24afbf] = 你撑得够久，久到她停下来真的开始讲解。“行吧，”她说，“你还凑合。”
# en: She wins, and you hit the floor hard enough to feel it tomorrow, but she shows you the trick on the way out, as if it were nothing.
opt.right.say.2 [cfe391] = 她赢了，你重重摔在地上，明天还会疼，但离开时她顺手把诀窍演示给你看，仿佛那不值一提。
# en: You end up on the floor with singed eyebrows. Lyra steps over you. "Ask better," she says.
opt.right.say.3 [a982db] = 你最后躺在地上，眉毛被燎焦了。莱拉从你身上跨过去。“下次问得好一点，”她说。

@event slice_stray_cold
# en: The Drift
title [b9d28f] = 寒流
# en: Cold drifts down the corridor like a tide coming in, and the torches lean away from it. {spell_level(ward) > 0: Your ward prickles at your fingertips.|You have nothing to hold it back.}
text [74bc38] = 寒意像涨潮一样漫过走廊，火把纷纷向一旁倾斜。{spell_level(ward) > 0: 你的护界在指尖隐隐刺痛。|你没有任何东西能挡住它。}
# en: A corridor at night where frost spreads across the flagstones toward a student holding a candle.
scene [e9d25c] = 夜里的一条走廊，霜正沿着石板向一个举着蜡烛的学生蔓延。
# en: Run for the stairs
opt.left.label [3e7200] = 往楼梯跑
# en: You make the stairs with frost in your hair. Behind you, the corridor sighs and is just a corridor again.
opt.left.say.1 [498ddb] = 你冲上楼梯时，头发里结满了霜。身后的走廊叹了口气，又变回了普通的走廊。
# en: Stand and study it
opt.right.label [0a0a0c] = 站住，研究它
# en: It isn't weather. It feels like being looked at, from somewhere far below. You write down everything before your hands warm up, and none of it makes sense yet.
opt.right.say.1 [791d24] = 这不是天气。更像是被注视着，从很深很深的下面。你趁双手还没回暖，把一切都记了下来，可眼下还一点也看不明白。
# en: You learn exactly one thing, which is how cold cold can be. Sister Amaranth wraps you in four blankets.
opt.right.say.2 [46b7a7] = 你只学到了一件事：冷能冷到什么地步。阿玛兰斯修女给你裹了四层毯子。
# en: Raise a ward
opt.up.label [d5a702] = 撑起护界
# en: Your ward flares, pale and steady. The cold breaks against it and slides away, the way a wave gives up on a rock.
opt.up.say.1 [e39cb8] = 你的护界亮起，苍白而稳定。寒流撞上它，滑开了，像浪头对一块礁石放弃了。

@event slice_late_lamps
# en: The Last Lamp
title [5ba6ee] = 最后一盏灯
# en: {~The library is emptying.|Rain on the high windows, and the library is emptying early.|Exam fever has filled the library all day; now, finally, it is emptying.} {~Footnote, the library cat, is asleep on the book you need|The book you need is on the top shelf, and the ladder squeaks|Someone has left a half-finished essay on your table, and a biscuit}, and the last lamp is yours if you want it.
text [d83f80] = {~图书馆渐渐空了。|雨打在高窗上，图书馆早早就空了。|考试热潮挤满了图书馆一整天；现在，终于，人渐渐散了。}{~图书馆的猫“脚注”趴在你要的那本书上睡着了|你要的那本书在最高一层，梯子吱呀作响|有人在你桌上留了一篇写了一半的论文，还有一块饼干}，最后一盏灯，你想要就是你的。
# en: The library at closing time, one desk still lit, a cat asleep on an open book.
scene [6a380e] = 闭馆时的图书馆，只剩一张书桌还亮着，一只猫睡在摊开的书上。
# en: Keep the lamp
opt.left.label [b4ddff] = 守着这盏灯
# en: {~You read until Footnote leaves in protest.|You read until the words swim.|You read until the night porter coughs pointedly.}
opt.left.say.1 [9dbe5e] = {~你读到“脚注”愤然离席。|你读到字都开始游动。|你读到守夜人意味深长地咳嗽。}
# en: Go to bed
opt.right.label [2fa817] = 回去睡觉
# en: {~You sleep like a stone. The book will still be there. So, probably, will Footnote.|You fall asleep before your head finds the pillow. You wake up knowing one thing you didn't, somehow.|You sleep well and dream of shelves. The lamp goes to someone who needed it more.}
opt.right.say.1 [edb97a] = {~你睡得像块石头。书还会在那里。“脚注”大概也是。|你头还没沾到枕头就睡着了。醒来时，不知怎么，你多懂了一件事。|你睡得很好，梦里全是书架。那盏灯留给了更需要它的人。}

@event slice_quarrel
# en: A Quarrel in the Courtyard
title [cdc8fb] = 庭院里的争执
# en: Kael and Lyra are facing each other in the courtyard, and the {season == "winter": snow|grass} between them is half {season == "winter": melted|scorched}, half frozen. "Say it again," Lyra says. Kael doesn't. He just looks at you.
text [d5c1cc] = 凯尔和莱拉在庭院里对峙，两人之间的{season == "winter": 雪|草地}一半{season == "winter": 融化|焦枯}、一半冻结。“再说一遍，”莱拉说。凯尔没有说。他只是看向你。
# en: Two students facing each other in a snowy courtyard, one breathing frost, the other with sparks at her fingertips.
scene [38c0d1] = 积雪的庭院里，两个学生面对面站着，一个呼出寒霜，另一个指尖迸着火星。
# en: Step between them
opt.left.label [f242e3] = 站到他们中间
# en: Lyra's sparks catch your sleeve, Kael's frost puts it out. They both stare at you. The fight, somehow, is over.
opt.left.say.1 [5ee694] = 莱拉的火星燎到你的袖子，凯尔的霜又把它扑灭。两人都盯着你。不知怎么，这场架就这么结束了。
# en: Walk past
opt.right.label [d5359c] = 径直走过
# en: Behind you, something cracks: ice, or temper. At dinner they sit at opposite ends of the hall.
opt.right.say.1 [d025e8] = 身后有什么裂开了：是冰，还是脾气。晚饭时，他们坐在大厅的两头。

@event slice_burned_letter
# en: Ashes in the Grate
title [4b34a6] = 壁炉里的灰
# en: Lyra is feeding a letter into the common-room fire, a corner at a time. Black seal. She doesn't look round. "It says 'well done'," she says. "It doesn't. I'm checking whether it burns better if I pretend."
text [847047] = 莱拉正把一封信一角一角地喂进公共休息室的壁炉。黑色封蜡。她没有回头。“信上写着‘做得好’，”她说，“其实没有。我在试试，假装有的话它会不会烧得更旺。”
# en: A fireplace where the corner of a letter with a black seal is curling into flame.
scene [e9282e] = 一座壁炉，一封盖着黑色封蜡的信的一角正卷进火焰里。
# en: Sit with her
opt.left.label [654e0a] = 陪她坐着
# en: You watch it burn together. "She's never said it," Lyra says, to the fire. "Not once." You don't say anything, and that seems to be right.
opt.left.say.1 [437064] = 你们一起看着它烧完。“她从没说过，”莱拉对着火说，“一次都没有。”你什么也没说，而这似乎正是对的。
# en: Make a joke
opt.right.label [5f1ec3] = 开个玩笑
# en: She almost smiles. Then she puts the rest of the letter in at once and leaves you with the smoke.
opt.right.say.1 [282f1d] = 她差点笑了。然后她把剩下的信一股脑儿丢进火里，留你和烟待在一起。

@event slice_hollow_whisper
# en: A Voice in the Water
title [b31d19] = 水中的声音
# en: At the lakeshore your reflection speaks before you do. "You're running low," it says, kindly. "{mana < 15: I could fill you up.|I could make you stronger.} Just say yes. Saying yes costs nothing."
text [f94671] = 在湖岸边，你的倒影先于你开口。“你快见底了，”它温和地说，“{mana < 15: 我可以把你填满。|我可以让你更强。}只要说‘好’。说‘好’什么都不花。”
# en: A student kneeling at the edge of a still lake at night, their reflection smiling when they are not.
scene [4bb1f8] = 夜里，一个学生跪在平静的湖边，水中的倒影在笑，而他自己并没有笑。
# en: Say yes
opt.left.label [c73ccb] = 说“好”
# en: Cold pours into you, generous and endless. When you stand, your reflection is a little slower to stand with you.
opt.left.say.1 [3ad748] = 寒意涌进你的身体，慷慨而无穷无尽。你站起来时，倒影慢了一拍才跟着站起来。
# en: Walk away
opt.right.label [96da1a] = 转身离开
# en: The reflection's smile stays on the water after you've gone. You don't look back. You can feel it not minding.
opt.right.say.1 [8bbf02] = 你走后，倒影的笑容还留在水面上。你没有回头。你能感觉到它并不在意。

@event slice_market_haggle
# en: The Spice Stall
title [8682c8] = 香料摊
# en: The stall-holder in the village market wants thirty crowns for {~a jar of starpepper|a twist of dragon-chilli|a pot of cliff-bee honey}. Mabel swears by it for colds. The stall-holder swears by his prices.
text [ed6115] = 小镇集市上的摊主要三十克朗卖{~一罐星辰胡椒|一束龙椒|一罐崖蜂蜜}。梅布尔发誓它治感冒有奇效。摊主则发誓他的价钱童叟无欺。
# en: A crowded village market stall heaped with jars of glowing spices and a stall-holder with an enormous moustache.
scene [ba55f9] = 拥挤的小镇集市摊位，堆满发光的香料罐，摊主留着一大把胡子。
# en: Haggle
opt.left.label [90048b] = 讨价还价
# en: Eight crowns and a compliment on your persistence. Mabel says you've been robbed, but only slightly.
opt.left.say.1 [ec3b10] = 八克朗，外加一句夸你有毅力。梅布尔说你被坑了，不过只坑了一点点。
# en: Fifteen crowns. He throws in a free sneeze's worth of pepper, which you did not want.
opt.left.say.2 [93bde1] = 十五克朗。他还白送你一个喷嚏的胡椒量——你并不想要。
# en: You pay full price and somehow promise to come back for more. He waves you off like a nephew.
opt.left.say.3 [3758d8] = 你付了全价，还不知怎么答应了下次再来买。他像送别侄子一样挥手送你走。
# en: Leave it
opt.right.label [3e2fed] = 算了
# en: You walk on. You catch a cold the next week, out of spite.
opt.right.say.1 [128e73] = 你走开了。下周你就感冒了，纯属赌气。

@event slice_wager
# en: The Tower Wager
title [013b2f] = 钟楼赌约
# en: Half the common room is betting on whether you can climb the clock tower before the bell. Corvin is holding the purse, which is either reassuring or not.
text [3371c6] = 半个公共休息室的人在赌你能不能在钟响前爬上钟楼。钱袋在科尔文手里——这让人放心，也可能不。
# en: A knot of students around a table where coins and a pocket watch are being stacked as bets.
scene [217f9f] = 一群学生围着一张桌子，桌上叠着当赌注的硬币和一块怀表。
# en: Climb
opt.left.label [2c7b2a] = 爬
# en: {~You make it with a heartbeat to spare.|The bell rings as your hand touches the top.} They carry you round the common room on a chair.
opt.left.say.1 [91cad2] = {~你提前一个心跳的工夫登了顶。|你的手碰到塔顶的那一刻，钟声响了。}他们把你放在椅子上，抬着绕公共休息室转了一圈。
# en: The bell rings when you're two-thirds up, and the caretaker has to talk you down with a ladder. They'll tell it for years.
opt.left.say.2 [e4a38c] = 你才爬了三分之二，钟就响了，最后是管理员架着梯子把你劝下来的。他们会把这事讲上好几年。
# en: Decline politely
opt.right.label [c5820d] = 礼貌地拒绝
# en: The crowd groans. Corvin pockets the purse thoughtfully and you decide not to ask.
opt.right.say.1 [3f87ed] = 人群一片哀叹。科尔文若有所思地把钱袋揣进兜里，你决定不问。

@event slice_frost_duel
# en: Frost Against Fire
title [63f7ba] = 霜与火
# en: Kael asks for a practice duel, which for him is an astonishing number of words. "Not to win," he adds. "I want to see what you do when it's cold."
text [4a4fd1] = 凯尔请你和他练一场决斗——对他来说，这已经是惊人的字数。“不是为了赢，”他补充道，“我想看看天冷的时候你会怎么做。”
# en: A duelling ring at dawn, frost spreading from one side and a faint warmth glowing from the other.
scene [8d420a] = 黎明时分的决斗场，一边蔓延着寒霜，另一边泛着微弱的暖光。
# en: Duel him straight
opt.left.label [a7dfd1] = 正面和他决斗
# en: You win by a whisker, breathing steam. Kael bows, and his hands, for once, are warm when he shakes yours. Half the duelling club, it turns out, was watching from the doorway.
opt.left.say.1 [07b3d4] = 你以毫厘之差获胜，呼出白汽。凯尔鞠了一躬，和你握手时，他的手难得是暖的。原来半个决斗社都在门口看着。
# en: A draw, of sorts: you're both on the ground. He laughs, a short surprised sound, and helps you up.
opt.left.say.2 [a850c0] = 算是平局：你们俩都倒在地上。他笑了，短促而意外的一声，然后把你拉了起来。
# en: He wins, gently. "You stopped when it got cold," he says. "Don't."
opt.left.say.3 [9548e4] = 他赢了，赢得很温和。“天一冷，你就停下了，”他说，“别停。”
# en: Decline; offer him tea instead
opt.right.label [3c2e56] = 婉拒，改请他喝茶
# en: He thinks about this for a long time. "Tea," he says. It freezes in his cup. You make him another.
opt.right.say.1 [c0affc] = 他想了很久。“茶，”他说。茶在他杯子里冻住了。你又给他泡了一杯。
# en: Answer with fire
opt.up.label [589d8f] = 以火回应
# en: Your flame meets his frost in a column of steam that fills the ring and brings half the corridor running. When it clears, Kael is smiling at you, properly, for the first time.
opt.up.say.1 [f78aa4] = 你的火焰迎上他的寒霜，一柱蒸汽填满了整个决斗场，引得半条走廊的人都跑了过来。散去时，凯尔正对你微笑——第一次真正地微笑。
